WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:04.960
Some sentences outlive the reason they were written.

00:00:05.210 --> 00:00:06.450
I catalogue them.

00:00:06.850 --> 00:00:10.287
Dr Anouk Mensah reads this year's wording against last year's,

00:00:10.437 --> 00:00:11.407
line by line.

00:00:11.807 --> 00:00:17.507
Over ten years, fourteen price-match promises gained one comma between them.

00:00:17.707 --> 00:00:19.717
Their fine print grew sixfold.

00:00:20.017 --> 00:00:23.117
A share house pins its quiet hours at ten,

00:00:23.267 --> 00:00:24.887
and keeps them past eleven.

00:00:25.187 --> 00:00:27.555
A library desk set up as interim

00:00:27.655 --> 00:00:30.485
is still interim after seven extensions.

00:00:30.985 --> 00:00:33.885
She's cited more often than most senior staff in her School.

00:00:34.885 --> 00:00:36.743
Nine hundred and sixty-five citations,

00:00:36.943 --> 00:00:39.093
and an h-index of twenty-five,

00:00:39.243 --> 00:00:41.743
from a hundred and ninety-four research outputs.

00:00:42.343 --> 00:00:44.703
Every new plan carries old words forward.

00:00:44.903 --> 00:00:46.423
I check what they still mean.

00:00:47.223 --> 00:00:48.443
Start reading on our website,

00:00:48.593 --> 00:00:49.903
get the latest on Bluesky,

00:00:50.053 --> 00:00:51.033
or drop us a line.
